From 15d5037f8cbd8944a18392ba50fbc312411e0511 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StonkGuy <68372320+StonkGuy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 00:09:28 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] JIT: report exec faults on unmapped guest memory as
 SEGV_MAPERR, like x86

Every instruction fetch that the frontend cannot read because the guest page is not executable
funnelled into NoExecOp, which raised SIGSEGV with a fixed si_code = SEGV_ACCERR and err =
PF_PROT|PF_USER|PF_INSTR (0x15): a protection fault. But the fetch can fail for two different
reasons, and the guest distinguishes them: the page is mapped without execute permission
(native: SEGV_ACCERR, err 0x15) or the page is not mapped at all (native: SEGV_MAPERR, err 0x14,
no PF_PROT). FEX reported the protection-fault form for both.

The distinction was already available where the fetch is checked: QueryGuestExecutableRange
returns a zero range both when the VMA lookup finds nothing and when it finds a mapped,
non-executable VMA. ExecutableRangeInfo gains a Mapped flag (default true, so the Windows and
offline-tool query paths keep their meaning), the VMA lookup sets it, the frontend records
HitUnmappedFetch on a failing range query for an unmapped address, and the new
DecodedBlockStatus::UNMAPPED_INST routes to a new UnmappedOp that raises SIGSEGV with
SEGV_MAPERR and err = PF_USER|PF_INSTR (0x14). Mapped-but-noexec keeps the old NoExecOp values.
Cost: one flag on the fault path only; decode of executable memory is unchanged.

Wine reads exactly these fields when it converts the signal to a Windows exception
(signal_x86_64.c signal_to_exception): si_code and the error code select the exception and its
parameters, so a recovery handler sees the right fault kind. A packer that recovers an execute
AV on a not-yet-mapped page via SEH is one consumer.

tests/segv-regs case 5 (jump to a page the guest munmapped): native x86-64 PASS; FEX reported
si_code=2 (ACCERR) err=0x15 (FAIL); with this change PASS, err=0x14, matching native. Cases 1-4
and 6 unchanged, all PASS, as on the 0001-0026 build. Regression set under the new build:
t_p0, t_term (160/160), seccomp-trap, maps-probe, tf-iret, signal-frame/-mask/-regs all PASS.

Upstream FEX main has the identical NoExecOp with the same hardcoded values (checked via
GitHub raw, 2026-10-10); there is no MAPERR path for instruction fetch anywhere in FEXCore.

Base: FEX-2610 14c92681 + patches 0001-0026.

