From 5618cb05e156bdf23442f56fc669bcc992821bfd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StonkGuy <68372320+StonkGuy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 04:30:32 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] JIT: report an undecodable instruction as #UD (trapno 6,
 ILL_ILLOPN)

An instruction the frontend cannot decode (BlockStatus INVALID_INST / BAD_RELOCATION: encodings that are invalid in
64-bit mode, bad LOCK use, ...) reached the guest as SIGILL with REG_TRAPNO 0 and si_code 0. On Linux x86-64 it is a
#UD: SIGILL, si_code ILL_ILLOPN (2), REG_TRAPNO 6 (arch/x86/kernel/traps.c handle_invalid_op -> do_error_trap). UD2 and
the unimplemented-instruction path (UnimplementedOp) in FEX already report 6/2; InvalidOp was the odd one out.

Consumer: Wine's segv_handler (also installed for SIGILL) switches on REG_TRAPNO; an unknown value is logged as
"Got unexpected trap 0" before the same EXCEPTION_ILLEGAL_INSTRUCTION is raised, so the NT exception is unchanged but the
log reports a spurious error per such instruction (seen from an anti-tamper runtime's probes). A program's own SIGILL
handler testing si_code or trapno saw the wrong values.

Cost: none; two constants in the generated Break reason.

tests/ud-regs (native x86-64 oracle): ud2, ud0, push es, pusha, daa, aam, LOCK on a register operand.

Upstream FEX main has the same InvalidOp (TrapNumber 0, si_code 0), checked via GitHub raw.

Base: FEX-2610 14c92681 + patches 0001-0026.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher.cpp | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

