From 18f972a49758691f0ff4015ecef044f798fde014 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StonkGuy <68372320+StonkGuy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 10:11:49 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] Signals: raise `int 3` (CD 03) as #BP and `int 4` as #OF,
 like Linux

INT imm8 reported every vector except 0x80 as a #GP with the vector in the error code. On x86-64 Linux the gates for
vectors 3 and 4 are user-callable: CD 03 is a #BP exactly like the one-byte INT3 (SIGTRAP, si_code SI_KERNEL, trapno 3,
RIP after the instruction) and CD 04 is #OF (SIGSEGV, si_code SI_KERNEL, trapno 4, RIP after the instruction). The other
vectors already matched (CD 00, 01, 21, 2d: SIGSEGV, trapno 13, error code vector<<3|2).

Consumer: Wine maps trapno 3 to EXCEPTION_BREAKPOINT and trapno 4 to EXCEPTION_INT_OVERFLOW; a Windows program that
uses the two-byte int 3 saw EXCEPTION_ACCESS_VIOLATION instead. Cost: none; chosen when the instruction is translated.

tests/invalid-ops (native x86-64 oracle): int3-cd03, int4-cd04.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
